{
  "id": "typescript-14-typing-javascript-libraries",
  "slug": "typing-javascript-libraries",
  "title": "Typing JavaScript libraries (@types and hand-written .d.ts)",
  "moduleId": "typescript-14-modules-and-declarations",
  "order": 4,
  "hook": "Untyped JS libs need **@types/***, bundled `.d.ts`, or hand **`declare module`**. Senior engineers check `package.json` types/exports before installing @types.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "What is this?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Read **.d.ts** for JS APIs. **@types/lodash** from DefinitelyTyped. Internal JS: **allowJs** + JSDoc `@ts-check`. **`declare module \"pkg\"`** shims untyped npm packages. Modern packages ship types via **exports.types**."
        },
        {
          "type": "glossary",
          "title": "Key terms",
          "entries": [
            {
              "term": "DefinitelyTyped",
              "longForm": "@types",
              "plainDefinition": "Community .d.ts on npm.",
              "example": "npm i -D @types/react"
            },
            {
              "term": ".d.ts",
              "longForm": "declaration file",
              "plainDefinition": "Type-only API description.",
              "example": "export function fn(): void"
            },
            {
              "term": "allowJs",
              "longForm": "checkJs",
              "plainDefinition": "Typecheck .js with JSDoc.",
              "example": "\"allowJs\": true"
            },
            {
              "term": "types field",
              "longForm": "package.json types",
              "plainDefinition": "Entry .d.ts for consumers.",
              "example": "\"types\": \"./dist/index.d.ts\""
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Why does it matter?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "@types version skew causes false errors. Enterprise SDKs need hand .d.ts. Publishing requires types in npm package."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "variant": "tip",
          "title": "Interview trap: @types vs bundled",
          "body": "Check package types/exports first — @types may be unnecessary or stub."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "How it works step by step",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "steps",
          "title": "Mental model",
          "items": [
            {
              "title": "Check bundled types",
              "body": "package.json types"
            },
            {
              "title": "Install @types",
              "body": "if separate"
            },
            {
              "title": "declare module shim",
              "body": "minimal .d.ts"
            },
            {
              "title": "JSDoc migration",
              "body": "allowJs gradual"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "diagram": {
            "type": "mermaid",
            "title": "Typing JS lib",
            "source": "flowchart TD\n  LIB --> Q{has d.ts?}\n  Q -->|yes| USE[bundled]\n  Q -->|@types| DT[install]\n  Q -->|no| AUTH[declare module]"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Code walkthrough",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "declare module shim",
            "code": "declare module \"legacy-analytics\" {\n  export function track(event: string, props?: Record<string, unknown>): void;\n}\nimport { track } from \"legacy-analytics\";",
            "explanation": "Shim untyped package."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "JSDoc in .js",
            "code": "// @ts-check\n/** @param {string} id @returns {Promise<{name:string}>} */\nexport async function loadUser(id) { return fetch(`/u/${id}`).then(r=>r.json()); }",
            "explanation": "Gradual JS typing."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "json",
            "label": "Publish types",
            "code": "{\n  \"types\": \"./dist/index.d.ts\",\n  \"exports\": { \".\": { \"types\": \"./dist/index.d.ts\", \"import\": \"./dist/index.js\" } }\n}",
            "explanation": "Consumers get types from package."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "Failure: stale @types",
            "code": "import { newMethod } from \"foo\"; // @types/foo old API",
            "explanation": "Version skew with JS lib."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Compare with JavaScript and C#",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "comparisonTable",
          "title": "Typing JavaScript libraries (@types and hand-written .d.ts) across languages",
